{%- comment -%}
  FAQ page.

  The design's nav sends FAQ to a homepage anchor rather than here, but the
  page itself stays: /pages/faqs is indexed and its handle is fixed by
  Decision #9. Deleting it would throw away long-tail search traffic — the FAQ
  answers real queries ("how long do pre-order wigs take") that a homepage
  section cannot rank for on its own, because a URL fragment is not indexed
  separately from the page it sits on.

  So this renders the same section the homepage does. One set of answers,
  edited once, appearing in both places — the section's settings are stored per
  section name, so there is no second copy to keep in sync.

  Assign this template to the FAQs page in Shopify admin:
    Content -> Pages -> FAQs -> Theme template -> "faqs"

  The hidden <h1> carries the page's own title so the document has exactly one
  first-level heading. The section's visible heading is an <h2>, which without
  this would be the topmost heading on the page — a hierarchy that starts at
  level 2. The page title and the section heading differ ("FAQs" against
  "Frequently Asked Questions"), so nothing is announced twice.
{%- endcomment -%}

<h1 class="visually-hidden">{{ page.title | escape }}</h1>

{% section 'ness-faq' %}
